# Freeze values for F15 DRAFT (2026-11-01). Copy to infra/freeze/freezes/F15.env, then select with: export KIT_FREEZE=F15
# Derived from infra/freeze/freezes/F14.env (same keys, same 13-name PREV_NAMES schema). Draft only: nothing is frozen, signed or run.
# Rules kept from the kit: no BOM, LF only, no quotes or trailing comment on FREEZE / FREEZE_COMMIT / GUEST_IP
# (freeze-guard.sh:8-11 reads those lines with sed; the mk-svc-config.py and mk-dr-config.py scripts split each non-comment line on "=").
# All comments are on their own lines.
#
# STATUS 2026-11-04: blockers 1 (commit chosen), 2 (ids on main), 3 and 5 (freeze home restored by Storage, 2026-11-01) and 4 (pair in kit commit 69feed6f) are cleared. Left: GUEST_IP check at run time (VM off now), Hyper-V checkpoint, the owner's kit chain.
# OPEN BLOCKERS. 10-freeze.sh must not run until each one is cleared (owners and steps in F15-prep.md):
#   1. FREEZE_COMMIT is still the placeholder. The owner selects a 40-hex commit that descends from 02f9fb71 and has HEAD on it.
#   2. The repo templates still carry F14's admission ids: infra/guest/serve-pi-service.g1.json:6 and serve-pi-service.route-probe.json:6.
#      10-freeze.sh step 3b refuses them.
#   3. The freeze home must sit at a short path: $OLDH/cf15 must be 28 bytes or less (10-freeze.sh:61 on PR #35; the dev kit has no such check).
#      F14's home /home/jeli2k/tbound-h.zfosIW gives 33 bytes.
#   4. infra/freeze/guest/05-runtime-swap.sh has no (02f9fb71, F15) measurer pair (lines 33-37). It is needed before 05, not before 10.
#   5. The F14 records must exist under $OLDH/f14 (check_prev_values, lib.sh:127-141). Today they are in the Ubuntu distro.
#
# Every PREV_* value below was looked up in evidence/F14/logs, then looked up again on the cited line (the line contains the value).

